# A Regime 1 central with both its hot and CGM pairs non-empty, and two Type 1 satellites holding
# CGM: galaxy[1] in the central's regime holds both pairs, galaxy[2] (Regime 0) holds its gas only
# in the pair its regime does not use.
# Shows the central migrating only its own gas (CGM into hot, I:170-176), the satellites keeping
# their CGM and metals (no satellite CGM added to the central, though the budget counts it), the
# ejected and ICS pooling unchanged, and the CGM safety checks not binding.
# Reachability: R4-reachable state (constructed values): a CGM-regime central gains hot gas from
# mergers (hot to hot) and a satellite keeps gas in the reservoir of an earlier regime; the R4
# reference holds both (Snap_32: 188 hot-regime centrals with both pairs non-empty, 88 CGM-regime
# satellites holding only hot gas).
# R4's flags: CGMrecipeOn 1 (par/R4.par:54); ReionizationOn 1, BaryonFrac 0.17,
# ReIncorporationFactor 0.19 and Reionization_z0/zr 8/7 as R3 (R4.par:51, :39, :72, :85-86).
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
routine infall_recipe

i32 params.ReionizationOn 1
i32 params.CGMrecipeOn 1
f64 params.BaryonFrac 0x3fc5c28f5c28f5c3  # 0.17000000000000001
f64 params.a0 0x3fbc71c71c71c71c  # 0.1111111111111111  (1/(1+Reionization_z0), z0 = 8)
